  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Ensuring the Delivery of Critical Humanitarian Assistance to Vulnerable Migrants in the Dominican Republic and The Bahamas.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Haiti is a major source country for emigrants, which over the years has resulted in a significant diaspora and a migrant population living in host countries such as The Bahamas and the Dominican Republic. As a direct consequence of the lack of regular pathways for migration and limited socioeconomic opportunities in their country of origin, many of these Haitian migrants are often forced take irregular pathways, risking their lives by embarking on dangerous journeys to reach more prosperous territories, including perilous sea and land crossings. In fact, Haitian migrants regularly face a wide range of protection issues, including human trafficking, smuggling, communicable diseases as well as lack of reintegration assistance for returnees and deportees. 
 
In close coordination with government authorities, the proposed intervention aims to ensure access to critical humanitarian assistance to vulnerable migrant communities, including Haitians, in The Bahamas and the Dominican Republic.</narrative>
  </description>
